        "text": "The first step to good portfolio management is setting your expectations. Are you risk averse and looking for a basket of investments protected from high volatility? Or do you want something riskier with potentially higher returns? In the short term, there are endless possibilities of how to put together your portfolio. It can be as complex or simple as you want, but it's recommended that you do some research and put in some thought. The amount of time you want to stay invested also matters. You could take a passive hands off strategy and leave your investments alone after you set them up. On the other hand, you can take an active approach, continuously buying and selling assets to profit.",
